    "audit.help.tab_usage": "Using the application",
    "audit.help.methodo": "<h1 class=\"heading-blue\">Methodology guide — ISO/IEC 27001:2022 audit</h1>\n<p class=\"text-muted\">Internal ISMS audit against ISO/IEC 27001:2022: clauses §4–§10 and Annex A</p>\n\n<h2>Purpose</h2>\n<p>This module supports an <strong>internal ISO/IEC 27001:2022 audit</strong>: assessment of the <strong>24 requirements of clauses §4–§10</strong> (the ISMS itself) and the <strong>93 Annex A controls</strong> (organizational, people, physical, technological). Each control carries a description, suggested <strong>audit questions</strong> and, where relevant, an <strong>HDS</strong> marker flagging points critical to the French health-data hosting certification.</p>\n\n<h2>Assessment statuses</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Score weight</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>Compliant</strong></td><td>The requirement is met, with supporting evidence</td><td>100%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Improvement opportunity</strong></td><td>Compliant but improvable</td><td>75%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Point of concern</strong></td><td>Short-term drift risk, no proven nonconformity</td><td>50%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Minor NC</strong></td><td>Isolated deviation, ISMS not compromised</td><td>25%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Major NC</strong></td><td>Missing or systemically failing requirement</td><td>0%</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>N/A</strong></td><td>Out of scope — excluded from scoring</td><td>—</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"help-tip\">The <strong>maturity score</strong> is the weighted average of assessed controls (excluding N/A): C&times;1 + IO&times;0.75 + PoC&times;0.5 + minor&times;0.25 + major&times;0. Grades: A &ge; 80%, B &ge; 65%, C &ge; 50%, D &ge; 35%, E below.</div>\n\n<h2>Documenting a finding</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Expected content</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>Criterion</strong></td><td>The reference requirement (clause or Annex A control)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Observation</strong></td><td>The observed fact, dated and verifiable</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Cause</strong></td><td>Root cause (organizational, technical, human)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Corrective action recommendation</strong></td><td>The auditor's proposal to close the gap</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Evidence images</strong> (screenshots, photos) can be attached to each finding.</p>\n\n<h2>From recommendation to corrective action</h2>\n<p>The <strong>recommendation</strong> is the auditor's opinion; the <strong>corrective action</strong> is the organization's commitment. From any finding, create a corrective action with an <strong>owner</strong> (directory picker), a <strong>due date</strong> and a status — prefilled from the recommendation, tracked in the <em>Corrective actions</em> panel, and pushed to <strong>Pilot</strong>'s consolidated action plan in suite deployments.</p>\n\n<h2>Document review</h2>\n<p>The document review lists <strong>34 documents expected</strong> of an ISMS (policies, SoA, risk register, management-review minutes…), each linked to the controls it feeds. Statuses: <strong>Received</strong>, <strong>Incomplete</strong>, <strong>Missing</strong>, <strong>N/A</strong>. A missing critical document shows the <strong>likely finding</strong> to carry over to the linked controls.</p>\n\n<h2>Audit schedule</h2>\n<p>The schedule generator spreads audited domains over the audit days (time slots, lunch break) and exports to CSV or Word.</p>\n\n<h2>Recommended approach</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1. Prepare</strong>: fill in the metadata (client, reference, dates, auditor, scope), build the schedule, send the document list</li>\n<li><strong>2. Document review</strong>: qualify received documents before the interviews</li>\n<li><strong>3. Interviews</strong>: walk the controls domain by domain using the audit questions</li>\n<li><strong>4. Qualify</strong> each observation with the right status and document the findings</li>\n<li><strong>5. Report</strong>: dashboard, Word/CSV exports, AI report</li>\n<li><strong>6. Follow up</strong>: create corrective actions and track them until findings are closed</li>\n</ul>",
    "audit.help.usage": "<h1 class=\"heading-blue\">Using the application</h1>\n<p class=\"text-muted\">Stored audits, data entry, exports and corrective actions</p>\n\n<h2>My audits</h2>\n<p>The <strong>File &rsaquo; My audits</strong> menu lists every stored audit: open, duplicate (start from a past audit), delete (administrator), <strong>import a JSON file</strong> produced by the online version, or create a new audit. The active audit is <strong>saved automatically</strong> on every change — there is no Save button.</p>\n<div class=\"help-tip\"><strong>Import from the online version</strong>: \"File &rsaquo; Open\" also accepts encrypted exports (AES-256) — decryption happens in the browser, then the audit is stored as a new one.</div>\n\n<h2>Assessing controls</h2>\n<p>Navigate by domain in the side rail (§4–§10, A.5–A.8). For each control: pick a <strong>status</strong>, fill in <strong>evidence</strong> and <strong>observations</strong>, and for findings the criterion / observation / cause / <strong>corrective action recommendation</strong> fields. The <strong>Questions</strong> button shows suggested interview questions (copyable); the paperclip attaches images.</p>\n\n<h2>Filters and search</h2>\n<p>The filter bar narrows by status, HDS marker or free text. The <strong>global search</strong> (magnifier) scans ids, titles, descriptions and observations across all controls.</p>\n\n<h2>Corrective actions</h2>\n<p>Create them from a finding (<em>Create a corrective action</em> button) or from the <strong>Corrective actions</strong> panel: title, description, <strong>owner picked from the directory</strong>, due date, status (To do / In progress / Done) and progress journal. In suite mode they feed Pilot's consolidated action plan.</p>\n\n<h2>Dashboard and exports</h2>\n<p>The dashboard aggregates counters, maturity score (A–E), distribution, per-domain radar and nonconformities. Exports: <strong>CSV</strong> (findings), <strong>Word</strong> (audit report), schedule CSV/Word, and <strong>AI report</strong> when the assistant is enabled.</p>\n\n<h2>Journal</h2>\n<p>The <strong>journal</strong> timestamps every change (statuses, fields, creations).</p>\n\n<h2>Language and theme</h2>\n<p>App-bar buttons: FR/EN switch (control catalogue included) and light/dark theme.</p>\n\n<h2>Features requiring AI</h2>\n<p>These features call a language model and are only available once AI is configured. They are <strong>optional</strong>: without configuration they are hidden or inactive and the rest of the module works normally.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Audit report generation</strong> &mdash; the menu entry stays hidden until AI is configured</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"help-tip\">Where to configure: in a standalone install, through the module's <strong>Settings &rarr; AI</strong> (your own API key). In the suite, keys are centralised by <strong>Pilot</strong> and pushed to the modules &mdash; nothing to enter here, and AI access is granted per user in the permissions matrix.</p>",
